## F. Pairing rules (to avoid sameness)
* Max 2 consecutive slides from the same family (A/B/C/D/E). Alternate chart ↔ text ↔ diagram.
* Every phase = divider (F3) → 1 context/diagram slide (D*) → 1–2 quantitative slides (C*/T*/C10) → 1 "implication/decision" slide (F5-style or D4).
* Use at most 3 different dark-red fills per slide; icons only from Think-cell sets (green outline) and recolored to `hal-deep`.
* Keep identical positions for title/subtitle/source across all slides (pixel-identical); vary only the content area.

